  "body": "Existing two-H cleanup compositions need the genuine unit receiver to physically release the second original H, then let the caller release the first and Copy-update the same original T. The C17 consumer also rejected legal current/sibling reads placed after startup Copy because its planner assumed the allocation match was immediately next.\n\nThis integrates the existing four-step terminal receiver consumer and the private repair that authenticates those pure T observations against the actual startup Copy handoff. Original root/field/incarnation/current facts, Allocation/Domain/owner, actual/formal, full range, closed loans and staged output remain mandatory. No source law, checker/public issuer/API/ABI change; optional receiver-internal five-step read and general CFG/owner/forwarding remain outside this increment.\n\nBase: `b2f22d39b61c0cf3ea18b7a1529fa8f0bf801be1`. Ordered merge retains original P738 history. Tree `d8567d3a12a8c1e35e51f21369c8e495d58a97d9` is exactly original P738 with the three adopted T1522 blobs substituted; all 7435 paths/modes/blobs checked. Diff from current main: 39 paths, 3990 additions/26 deletions, with no T/tooling/workflow/governance diff. Historical PR1526 remains unchanged.\n\nValidation on this integration:\n- Six positive sources: CHECK → genuine MACHINE/owned → C17/public API byte agreement, matching their original generated C.\n- 18 actual strict GCC/Clang O2 native runs, including H0/H1/H2, zero/nonzero, selected ASan/UBSan, original free order and same-T old/current/sibling.\n- Four source negatives, four artifact negatives, rollback and pristine retries; four host OOM sites/12 fault-retry cases including named no-clobber.\n- Fresh GCC Release and pinned Clang ASan frontend/probe builds; all 18 p1517 and 10 p1529 tests registered. Full local CTest sweep not run; natural Required6 + EARLY2 pending.\n\nDRAFT / HOLD. Publication gate was the actual post-T main FULL44422430481 + PARTIAL44422430436, exact b2f/attempt1/all six successful jobs. No manual CI retry/dispatch. Independent review and READY/merge remain Coordination decisions. Finite capability success does not establish comparative UB-audit locality; Product GO remains paused.\n\nScope, original FIRST/RED, provenance, per-file blob audit and final CI evidence: #1531.",
